 "summary": "No second-kind Bessel function exists in Mathlib (only `Complex.besselJ`, with the second kind listed as a TODO), Physlib/PhyslibAlpha (`besselSq`/`besselJ1` only), or TauCeti, and the PR reuses the existing first-kind API (`sphericalBesselJ_add_two_of_ne_zero`, `deriv_sphericalBesselJ_of_ne_zero`, `sphericalBesselJ_zero/_one`, `sinc_of_ne_zero`) for the cross product and Wronskian. The one private lemma is a required induction base case, not a restatement of public API.",
